ics Department at GEIMS: Nurturing Excellence in Musculoskeletal Health and Compassionate Healing<\/strong><\/p>","text_color":"#65CC33","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"Roboto","typography_font_size":{"unit":"px","size":"21","sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"400"},"elements":[],"widgetType":"text-editor"},{"id":"1be8986","elType":"widget","settings":{"text":"Divider","color":"#65CC33","weight":{"unit":"px","size":"2","sizes":[]},"gap":{"unit":"px","size":"2","sizes":[]}},"elements":[],"widgetType":"divider"},{"id":"95d683c","elType":"widget","settings":{"editor":"<p>Step into the realm of advanced orthopedic education at the Orthopedics Department of Graphic Era Institute of Medical Sciences (GEIMS). Our commitment to innovation, education, and community service defines an environment where academic brilliance seamlessly integrates with compassionate patient care.<\/p><p><strong>Cutting-Edge Facilities:<\/strong><\/p><p>Our state-of-the-art facilities immerse students in advanced orthopedic education, mirroring real-world settings. Equipped with modern diagnostic tools, surgical suites, and rehabilitation centers, the department ensures hands-on experience, preparing students for the dynamic challenges of orthopedic practice.<\/p><p><strong>Expert Faculty and Mentorship:<\/strong><\/p><p>At the heart of our orthopedic excellence lies a team of renowned faculty members\u2014skilled orthopedic professionals, passionate educators, and mentors. Their expertise spans various orthopedic specialties, offering students a comprehensive learning experience. Mentorship extends beyond clinical skills to instill a commitment to ethical practice, continuous learning, and patient-centered care.<\/p><p><strong>Comprehensive Curriculum:<\/strong><\/p><p>Delve into a meticulously crafted curriculum that provides a thorough understanding of orthopedic principles and practices. From musculoskeletal anatomy to cutting-edge surgical techniques, our curriculum ensures graduates are not only proficient but also adaptable to the evolving field of orthopedics.<\/p>","text_color":"#7A7A7A"},"elements":[],"widgetType":"text-editor"}],"isInner":"1"},{"id":"5aefa4e","elType":"widget","settings":[],"elements":[],"widgetType":"spacer"},{"id":"3c0f806","elType":"container","settings":{"flex_direction":"column","content_width":"full","width":{"unit":"%","size":"33.3333"},"flex_gap":{"column":"10","row":"10","isLinked":"1","unit":"px","size":"10"},"background_background":"classic","background_color":"#3A3A3A","padding":{"unit":"px","top":"20","right":"20","bottom":"20","left":"20","isLinked":""},"_flex_align_self":"flex-start","_flex_size":"none","_flex_grow":"0","_flex_shrink":"0","sticky":"top","sticky_offset":"100","sticky_effects_offset":"100","sticky_parent":"yes","animation":"slideInUp","animation_duration":"fast"},"elements":[{"id":"e7017ae","elType":"widget","settings":[],"elements":[],"widgetType":"spacer"},{"id":"496f51d","elType":"widget","settings":{"title":"Department Info","header_size":"h5","align":"center","title_color":"#FFFFFF"},"elements":[],"widgetType":"heading"},{"id":"0cc6981","elType":"widget","settings":{"editor":"<p>Department of Orthopedics<\/p>","align":"center","text_color":"#65CC33","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"Roboto","typography_font_weight":"700"},"elements":[],"widgetType":"text-editor"},{"id":"c5b2f2e","elType":"widget","settings":{"editor":"<p>Graphic Era Institute of Medical Sciences<br \/>16th Milestone, Chakrata Rd, Dehradun, Uttarakhand 248008<\/p>","align":"center","text_color":"#FFFFFF","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"Roboto","typography_font_size":{"unit":"px","size":"14","sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"500","typography_letter_spacing":{"unit":"px","size":"0","sizes":[]}},"elements":[],"widgetType":"text-editor"},{"id":"951cf24","elType":"widget","settings":[],"elements":[],"widgetType":"spacer"}],"isInner":"1"}],"isInner":fal